building yupiter
================

Requirements
------------

  * GNU Make 3.82 or newer.
  * POSIX shell, sed, awk, install, nm, readelf.
  * GNU or Clang C and C++ compilers.
  * A C++23 compiler with freestanding standard library support
    (libstdc++ from GCC 13; libc++ and MSVC do not).
  * Linux on aarch64 or x86_64.

No network access, package manager or third-party dependency is needed.


Quick start
-----------

    ./configure
    make
    make check
    make install

"make" builds libyupiter.a and libyupiter.so by default.  The build
tree is always build/ in the source directory.  make clean removes it.


Configure options
-----------------

Run ./configure --help.  Common options:

    --cc, --cxx            Compiler selection.
    --build-type           debug, relwithdebinfo, release.
    --heap-size            Arena size in bytes (>= 64).
    --enable-static        yes/no.
    --enable-shared        yes/no.
    --enable-tests         yes/no.
    --arch                 aarch64 or x86_64.

Unknown build types, empty arenas and unsupported architectures are
rejected at configure time.


Flags
-----

The library is freestanding C++23: -ffreestanding, -fno-builtin,
-fno-stack-protector, -fno-exceptions, -fno-rtti,
-fno-threadsafe-statics, -fvisibility=hidden.  The tests are hosted
C17/C++17 with the same warnings but no freestanding restrictions,
because they link the archive and the startup file.

The public header and C tests are ISO C17 with extensions off; the
implementation is ISO C++23 with extensions off.  The C++ compatibility
test is C++17 on purpose.


Freestanding check
------------------

archive_is_freestanding inspects the archive and shared object for
references to a C library or C++ runtime, mangled names, and
initializer sections.  The shared object must also have no undefined
dynamic symbols and no NEEDED entry.  See test/check-freestanding.sh.